From: Fizban <35464167+Fiztba@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 04:31:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 49/52] Cache idle IOP thread selection until scheduling
 changes

Frequent host-clock reconciliation repeatedly scanned every IOP thread while all were asleep or delayed. Cache the absence of Ready threads and the earliest delayed wake, invalidate that result before every kernel scheduling mutation, and rescan at the exact wake cycle. Combine delayed-thread promotion and priority selection in one pass while preserving priority and thread-ID ordering.

Native Windows validation passes 48,299 exact kernel, CPU, RAM and allocator checks against the unchanged implementation, the four IOP suites and the authored audio-clock regression. Mechanical controls detect missing mutation invalidation and an incorrect wake-boundary comparison.
